  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001: pca_n2000, resnet50, concat, singleprofile, multimodal) yielded ~52.7% accuracy, a weak baseline. The most impactful single-variable question is whether replacing the linear PCA RNA encoder (pca_n2000) with a learned, context-aware encoder (scgpt) substantially improves representation quality. config_043 changes only the RNA encoder (pca_n2000 → scgpt) while holding image encoder (resnet50), fusion (concat), and profile setting (singleprofile) identical to config_001, giving a clean A/B comparison. This is the best use of experiment 2 because: (1) the RNA encoder is likely the most informative modality for cellular profiling, so its quality is the highest-leverage design choice; (2) a single-variable change from the baseline isolates the effect of the encoder upgrade; and (3) with 8 experiments remaining, establishing whether scgpt is meaningfully better than PCA early will guide whether to invest subsequent experiments in scgpt-based multimodal/multiprofile configurations."
}

